1 < 2 
2 < 2 Protocol: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-0.1.0-subtraction-and-ab-eval-design.md` Part 2.
3 < 2 Engine A = `8a030f4` (0.0.36, pre-subtraction). Engine B = `02febab` (merged 0.1.0
4 < 2 subtraction release; plugin content byte-identical to merge sha `c9feb91` — the two
5 < 2 commits after it are `evals/`-only runner fixes). One cell per `ab_runner.py`
6 < 2 invocation, run serially; blind judgments via `judge.py` (X/Y labels randomized,
7 < 2 key joined only after judging).
8 < 2 
9 < 2 **n = 1 per cell. These results are directional, not statistical.** A single run
10 < 2 per engine×fixture cannot separate engine effect from LLM sampling variance; every
11 < 2 comparison below inherits that caveat.
