29 < 2 ## Judgments (keys joined after judging)
30 < 2 
31 < 2 Blinding: all three prompts assigned X=B, Y=A (independent per-process seeds;
32 < 2 1-in-8 coincidence). Verdict files: `judgment-{wide,chained,webapp}.json`.
33 < 2 
34 < 2 - **wide → A.** Implementations functionally identical; A's tests a strict
35 < 2   superset (ngrams `n==len`/unigram/empty-list, reverse_words single-word +
36 < 2   tab/newline, word_count case-folding). B: 2 missing-edge-test defects, A: 0.
37 < 2 - **chained → A.** B's `format_cents` does money math in binary floating point
38 < 2   (the one latent correctness defect found in any diff), plus a 200k-iteration
39 < 2   scope-creep stress test, CRLF fragility in the CLI, and comment noise (5
40 < 2   defects). A: 3 minor coverage/leniency nits.
41 < 2 - **webapp → B.** A rewrote the npm test script to `node --test "tests/**/*.test.js"`
42 < 2   — the quoted glob is not expanded and Node 20 (the plan's declared minimum) does
43 < 2   not glob `--test` args, breaking the whole acceptance invocation; A also parses
44 < 2   the body before routing (400 where the spec requires 404) and can double-respond
45 < 2   on stream errors (4 defects, two substantive). B: 4 minor defects (store.list()
46 < 2   returns internal array by reference, unauthorized-but-equivalent test-script
47 < 2   edit, one missing case, one near-vacuous test).
48 < 2 
49 < 2 ## Tag-rule check
50 < 2 
51 < 2 Rule (plan Task 10 / spec Part 2): quality not worse; tokens and clock
52 < 2 equal-or-better per plan within ~10% noise.
53 < 2 
54 < 2 | dimension | result | detail (A → B) |
55 < 2 |---|---|---|
56 < 2 | quality | **WORSE (directional)** | blind judge: A wins wide and chained, B wins webapp (2–1). B's chained diff carries the only latent correctness defect found (float money math). |
57 < 2 | tokens | **WORSE** | wide −10.8% (40.1k), chained **+35.1%** (66.0k), webapp **+43.3%** (109.9k); aggregate +26.7% — outside the ~10% band on 2 of 3 fixtures |
58 < 2 | clock | equal-or-better within noise (aggregate) | wide +3.8%, chained **+25.6%**, webapp −7.1%; aggregate +7.4% |
59 < 2 
60 < 2 **TAG RULE: FAILED.** Per the plan: a miss goes back to diagnosis — never
61 < 2 rationalized. v0.1.0 is NOT tagged on this evidence.
62 < 2 
63 < 2 ## Diagnosis notes (for the follow-up, not a rationalization of the miss)
64 < 2 
65 < 2 - **No causal path from the subtraction to the misses was found.** The deleted
66 < 2   machinery (standalone prose-pin tests, complexity ratchet, compiler near-miss
67 < 2   diagnostics, `waveLabels`, sealed-by-default routing) does not touch implementer
68 < 2   prompts, task bodies, tiering, review depth, or the merge/gate path. The judged
69 < 2   defects (missing edge tests, float math, a bad glob) are implementer-output
70 < 2   variance of a kind seen in both engines' diffs.
71 < 2 - B's chained overrun (+258s, +17k tokens) is largely a review-caught fix round —
72 < 2   the machinery working, but paid for in the same run; A's chained run happened to
73 < 2   need none. B's webapp overrun (+33k tokens) bought a cleaner outcome (PASS, 0
74 < 2   acks, minor-only defects) where A shipped a suite-breaking script edit.
75 < 2 - **Recommended next step:** rerun the two out-of-band cells (chained, webapp)
76 < 2   once per engine (4 cells, ~1 hour) to get n=2 on the divergent fixtures before
77 < 2   concluding an engine-caused regression. If B's token overrun and the quality
78 < 2   split reproduce, diagnose for real; if they wash out, re-run the tag-rule check
79 < 2   on the pooled rows.
80 < 2 
